<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-bipectinata-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila bipectinata Turing wavelength at 1.92 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 76.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 implements the continuous Turing wavenumber for Schnakenberg kinetics on a periodic 15.36 µm patch and renders a 13-frame 640×480 melanin overlay. Expressivity, ablation, specimen segmentation, and dispersion GoF are present in the script but were not yet the basis of the score. Overall is the weighted mean of the seven dimension scores below. Overall 76.4/100 (faithfulness 74.6, reproducibility 80.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scipy 1.18.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 72, Morphometric validation 70, Source and data traceability 84, Code-to-model traceability 78, Reproducibility package 80. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_bipectinata_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-bipectinata-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/gif, 3266791 B, 640×480 px, 13 frames, artifact_sha256 1c0014b74396d41aea1c5fed8b925dfed4668c3d0198033eb7281e541fec2fdc (sha256 1c0014b74396d41aea1c5fed8b925dfed4668c3d0198033eb7281e541fec2fdc), spec_fingerprint d5f22a094ff81c9bfb8cec455feea78ef577fb724b6dfb1571cde0d7f6d97c6c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d5f22a094ff81c9bfb8cec455feea78ef577fb724b6dfb1571cde0d7f6d97c6c; artifact_sha256: 1c0014b74396d41aea1c5fed8b925dfed4668c3d0198033eb7281e541fec2fdc. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite critical wavenumber from a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg 1979 gives the kinetics a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v. | Kopp & True 2002 and Mishra & Singh 2006 describe D. bipectinata paired oblique sex combs. They do not report a 1.92 µm wavelength.; reconstructed_in_script: gamma is solved so the continuous focal wavelength is 1.92 µm at D_u = 0.0504 µm^2/s and delta = 31.5. | Predecessor and successor wavelengths follow from D_u factors 25/16 and 16/25 at geological age 0 Ma.; transfer_boundary: The gallery JPEG is a stand-in specimen, not a micrograph of the 1.92 µm field.; does_not_claim: That 1.92 µm was measured by Kopp, Mishra, or Hurtado-Gonzales. | That D. biarmipes and D. buzzatii are stratigraphic ancestors. | That the catalog DOI 10.1111/j.1525-142X.2005.05044.x is a Kopp paper. Crossref maps it to Kerr, Roalson & Rodgers 2005 on zebrafish myostatin.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add a finite-amplitude equal-diffusion ablation and report its amplification against the Turing run.",
        "remediation needed: Add an explicit seven-point D_u sweep and show that lambda increases with sqrt(D_u).",
        "remediation needed: Report even-mode Pearson r, held-out odd-mode RMSE, and a KS distance, each with value distinct from its reference.",
        "remediation needed: Segment the pinned specimen image at two contrast thresholds and report coherency." ;
    pk:hasScore 7.64e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

